      },
      "message": "feat(post)!: Air coolant mode, machine default coolant, editor keeps coolant codes\n\nAn operation can ask for Air (CoolantMode::Air, PARAM Coolant air): every\npost that reads the ask resolves it from the machine's Air / Air blast\nentry, or refuses it by name. carvera.cps now declares coolantModes and\nposts the op's ask instead of \"the first Flood entry\", so a profile that\nkept the seeded Flood M8 beside an Air M7 no longer posts M8 for air.\ntormach.cps takes the generic flood law (no air/mist code for a flood\nop). A new op starts on its machine's default coolant (Air on an\nAir-only Carvera). The machine file editor adds a coolant with its code,\ncan remove any coolant (the seeded Flood included), lays its controls\nout so a narrow pane never clips them, and refuses a codeless coolant by\nname before any save.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: a Flood op on a machine whose only coolant is Air (an\nop on the shipped Carvera saved before this change) is refused by name\ninstead of posting the air code M7; pick Air for the op.\n\nFixes #869\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
